<PubmedArticle><MedlineCitation Status="PubMed-not-MEDLINE" Owner="NLM"><PMID Version="1">42780177</PMID><DateCompleted><Year>2026</Year><Month>09</Month><Day>24</Day></DateCompleted><DateRevised><Year>2026</Year><Month>09</Month><Day>24</Day></DateRevised><Article PubModel="Electronic"><Journal><JournalIssue CitedMedium="Internet"><PubDate><Year>2026</Year><Month>Sep</Month><Day>16</Day></PubDate></JournalIssue><Title>medRxiv : the preprint server for health sciences</Title><ISOAbbreviation>medRxiv</ISOAbbreviation></Journal><ArticleTitle>Real-World Effectiveness of Maternal RSVpreF Vaccination and Durability of Infant Protection.</ArticleTitle><ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">2026.09.15.26363141</ELocationID><ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.64898/2026.09.15.26363141</ELocationID><Abstract><AbstractText>In this test-negative study, the effectiveness of the maternal RSVpreF vaccine among infants &lt;6 months was 73.9% against medically attended respiratory syncytial virus (RSV) infection and 86.3% against RSV-associated hospitalization. Maternal RSVpreF and nirsevimab had comparable initial effectiveness, but effectiveness of RSVpreF waned approximately 1.7 times more rapidly.</AbstractText></Abstract><AuthorList CompleteYN="Y"><Author ValidYN="Y"><LastName>Xu</LastName><ForeName>Hanmeng</ForeName><Initials>H</Initials><Identifier Source="ORCID">0009-0000-2805-0171</Identifier></Author><Author ValidYN="Y"><LastName>Aparicio-Llorente</LastName><ForeName>Camila</ForeName><Initials>C</Initials></Author><Author ValidYN="Y"><LastName>Wats</LastName><ForeName>Aanchal</ForeName><Initials>A</Initials><Identifier Source="ORCID">0000-0002-2706-9660</Identifier></Author><Author ValidYN="Y"><LastName>Araujo</LastName><ForeName>Barbara L</ForeName><Initials>BL</Initials></Author><Author ValidYN="Y"><LastName>Ganem</LastName><ForeName>Julia Moniz</ForeName><Initials>JM</Initials></Author><Author ValidYN="Y"><LastName>Oliva</LastName><ForeName>Isabela O</ForeName><I